# RRAY (chief + 4 marginal rays), PRAY (8 pupil-ring rays), TPR (trace the found rays), FSR (the ray
# nearest a fractional source position) on the manual's Cassegrain with exit pupil (cmdref: Ray Tracing).
# TPR (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (e), fixed 2026-10-17): it printed RayPosHist, filled only when the deck
# declares SaveRayPosH= Y (every position 0 on this deck), and after RRAY it also traced "ray 0" from
# the slots RRAY leaves empty (NaN with the key).  It now prints the position CTRACE leaves at the end
# element and skips empty slots.  The numbers below are what the pre-fix TPR printed WITH
# SaveRayPosH= Y (b81021f, ifx): ray 63 (-9.075851181705730E-11, 8.250726490910409E-12, 1.5), ray 108
# x -5.768541200268373E-11, the chief (0, 0, 1.5).
# B.2 (2026-10-17): PRAY's first ring point read srp(1)=9.0 (the other seven sit at 0.9), so its +x
# ray was RRAY's edge ray 63 (1.6923) while -x landed at -1.3846 (ray 53); now ray 62 at 1.3846.  RRAY
# left slots 6..9 holding a previous PRAY's rays, and TPR traced them (53 19 12 26) as RRAY's; the
# last leg (PRAY, RRAY, TPR) pins that they are cleared.  FSR (all three commands) left ifRayPrint
# .TRUE., so the next OPD printed every ray's segments; the OPD after FSR pins that it does not
# (TPR clears the flag itself, so the OPD must come before it).  All
# three legs are red on 56de986's build.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CassWithExitPupil.in
rray
tpr
pray
tpr
fsr
0.5,0
opd 6
/null
rray
tpr
# EXPECT: Source aperture diameter =\s+4\.0000
# EXPECT: Ref\. ray XY offsets from chief ray:\s+1\.6923,\s+-0\.1538,\s+ID =\s+63
# EXPECT: Reference ray indices \(chief \+ 4 marginal\) =\s+1\s+63\s+122\s+52\s+4
# EXPECT: Ref\. ray XY offsets from chief ray:\s+1\.0769,\s+1\.0769,\s+ID =\s+108
# EXPECT: Ref\. ray XY offsets from chief ray:\s+0\.7692,\s+-0\.1538,\s+ID =\s+60
# EXPECT: Ray id:\s+60
# EXPECT: Ref\. ray XY offsets from chief ray:\s+1\.3846,\s+-0\.1538,\s+ID =\s+62\s+Ref\. ray XY offsets from chief ray:\s+1\.0769,\s+1\.0769,\s+ID =\s+108
# EXPECT: Ray id:\s+60[\s\S]*TPR ray 4 at element 6:
# EXPECT-NOT: Ray id:\s+60[\s\S]*TPR ray (53|19|12|26) at
# EXPECT: RMS OPD error is
# EXPECT-NOT: segment from Element
# EXPECT-NOT: Need to run RRAY
# EXPECT: TPR ray 1 at element 6:\s+0\.0+E\+00\s+0\.0+E\+00\s+1\.50+E\+00
# EXPECT: TPR ray 63 at element 6:\s+-?\d\.\d+E-(1\d|[2-9]\d)\s+-?\d\.\d+E-(1\d|[2-9]\d)\s+1\.50+E\+00
# EXPECT: TPR ray 108 at element 6:\s+-?\d\.\d+E-(1\d|[2-9]\d)\s
# EXPECT-NOT: TPR ray 0 
# EXPECT-NOT: NaN
# EXPECT-NOT: RayPosHist
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
